---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Security - CloudDroid" description="CloudDroid security practices: encryption, audit logging, access controls, and compliance measures.">
  <div class="bg-slate-light py-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-navy mb-4">Security</h1>
      <p class="text-slate text-lg">How CloudDroid protects your data, instances, and accounts.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-16">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-navy mb-4">Encryption</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <div class="bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-5">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-navy mb-1">In Transit</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate">All web traffic is encrypted with TLS 1.3. API and dashboard connections require HTTPS.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-5">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-navy mb-1">At Rest</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate">Database files and stored data are protected with AES-256-grade storage controls on the host layer.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-navy mb-4">Audit Logging</h2>
        <p class="text-slate mb-4">CloudDroid maintains structured audit logs for security-relevant events. Logged events include authentication, instance actions, administrative changes, and policy-relevant system events.</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-slate space-y-2">
          <li>Login, logout, and failed authentication attempts</li>
          <li>Instance start, stop, restart, and deletion</li>
          <li>User and role changes</li>
          <li>Password and 2FA changes</li>
          <li>Checkout and subscription events</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-navy mb-4">Access Controls</h2>
        <p class="text-slate mb-4">Access to production systems and customer data is restricted. Authentication uses session-based access with HTTP-only cookies, optional TOTP-based two-factor authentication, and active session management.</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-slate space-y-2">
          <li>Role-based access for administrative functions</li>
          <li>Session inventory and remote revocation</li>
          <li>Rate limiting on sensitive endpoints</li>
          <li>Request size limits and input validation</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-navy mb-4">Operational Practices</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <div class="bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-5">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-navy mb-1">Monitoring</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate">Instance metrics, alerting, and anomaly detection are available in the dashboard.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-5">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-navy mb-1">Incident Response</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate">Security events are logged and reviewable. Customers can report issues to support@clouddroid.eu.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-5">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-navy mb-1">Data Handling</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate">Payment data is handled by Dodo Payments. CloudDroid does not store raw card data.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-5">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-navy mb-1">Dependencies</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate">Runtime dependencies are reviewed and kept minimal. Production builds exclude development tooling.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-navy mb-4">Reporting a Security Issue</h2>
        <p class="text-slate">If you believe you have found a security vulnerability, please report it to <a href="mailto:support@clouddroid.eu" class="text-navy underline">support@clouddroid.eu</a>. We ask that responsible disclosure be followed.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
